waiting for pka0.7.0.2000.0 to start...
waiting for pka0.7.0.2000.0 to start...
(boot dka0.0.0.2000.0 -flags a)
=====>8=====

The system then just seems to hang and never boots off the disk.   
There are no problems booting from power on or from a hard reset.   
This leads me to believe that the shutdown under netbsd-5 is perhaps  
leaving the hardware in an unclean/inconsistent state that prevents a  
clean boot.  (Like I said, this only started happening post-upgrade.)

